in all of the Jewish hymn book.

186
00:18:21,280 --> 00:18:24,340
Psalm 16 is a very clear messianic hymn.

187
00:18:24,340 --> 00:18:30,260
And the demon calls Jesus by the title that is used for the Holy One of God.

188
00:18:30,260 --> 00:18:33,420
The demon acknowledges Jesus.

189
00:18:33,420 --> 00:18:35,420
He commands it to come out.

190
00:18:35,420 --> 00:18:38,420
And news begins to spread quickly.

191
00:18:38,420 --> 00:18:45,580
We went from Jesus in the wilderness to John the Baptist is put in prison.

192
00:18:45,580 --> 00:18:48,540
And everything begins to spiral out of control for the Jews.

193
00:18:48,540 --> 00:18:51,760
Could this be the time the Messiah is coming?

194
00:18:51,760 --> 00:18:57,160
Jesus announces the kingdom, calls a few disciples, begins to teach with authority in the synagogues.

195
00:18:57,160 --> 00:19:00,340
A demon calls him by a messianic name.

196
00:19:00,340 --> 00:19:02,260
Jesus casts out the demon.

197
00:19:02,260 --> 00:19:07,600
And now you can understand why news about him is spreading throughout the region of Galilee.

198
00:19:07,600 --> 00:19:11,080
I told you, it was fast-paced, action-packed.

199
00:19:11,080 --> 00:19:13,660
Mark is quickly giving the people what they want.

200
00:19:13,660 --> 00:19:17,820
Anticipation is building and the news begins to spread.

201
00:19:17,820 --> 00:19:19,040
Verse 29.

202
00:19:19,640 --> 00:19:24,220
As soon as they left the synagogue, they went in with James and John to the home of Simon and Andrew.

203
00:19:24,220 --> 00:19:28,880
Simon's mother-in-law was in bed with the fever, and they immediately told Jesus about her.

204
00:19:28,880 --> 00:19:32,880
So he went to her, took her hand, and helped her up.

205
00:19:32,880 --> 00:19:35,060
The fever left her, and she began to wait on him.

206
00:19:35,060 --> 00:19:41,040
That evening, after sunset, the people brought to Jesus all the sick and demon-possessed.

207
00:19:41,680 --> 00:19:46,760
The whole town gathered at the door, and Jesus healed many who had various diseases.

208
00:19:46,760 --> 00:19:54,220
He also drove out many demons, but he would not let the demons speak, because they knew who he was.

209
00:19:54,220 --> 00:19:58,560
Snowball just continues to roll down the hill for Mark here.

210
00:19:59,060 --> 00:20:00,300
It's picking up speed.

211
00:20:00,300 --> 00:20:03,040
Remember, Jesus came straight out of his solitude.

212
00:20:03,040 --> 00:20:13,120
In the Gospel of Mark, Jesus comes straight out of his 40-day solitude with Jesus into this fast-paced, ministry-action-oriented gospel.

213
00:20:13,120 --> 00:20:20,020
He's healing sick people in front of the entire town, and everyone was thinking the same thing.

214
00:20:20,020 --> 00:20:21,460
The time has come.

215
00:20:21,960 --> 00:20:22,400
Him.

216
00:20:22,400 --> 00:20:24,920
This is the time.

217
00:20:24,920 --> 00:20:30,980
We're not even through the first chapter of Mark yet, and, like, the whole crowd is ready to go, right?

218
00:20:30,980 --> 00:20:32,260
Like, let's do this thing.

219
00:20:32,260 --> 00:20:33,300
The Messiah is here.

220
00:20:33,300 --> 00:20:38,260
And this is where the story begins to take a subtle but important turn.

221
00:20:38,260 --> 00:20:45,940
Verse 35, after all of that fast-paced ministry, after Jesus beginning to enter the synagogue and teach with authority,

222
00:20:45,940 --> 00:20:48,960
after casting out demons and healing the sick in front of a whole crowd,

223
00:20:49,160 --> 00:20:50,140
I'm going to give you a bottle of water.

224
00:20:50,140 --> 00:20:51,600
I'm going to keep profiting.

225
00:20:51,600 --> 00:20:54,540
Brian's working on it.

226
00:20:54,540 --> 00:20:55,820
Profit.

227
00:20:55,820 --> 00:20:56,900
We have a prophet in our midst.

228
00:20:56,900 --> 00:20:59,580
All right.

229
00:20:59,580 --> 00:21:03,060
After all of that, this is where we pick up.

230
00:21:03,060 --> 00:21:06,040
Very early in the morning, while it was still dark,

231
00:21:06,040 --> 00:21:11,280
Jesus got up and left the house, and he went off to a solitary place.

232
00:21:11,280 --> 00:21:14,580
That's the same word for the desert, aremos, solitude.

233
00:21:14,580 --> 00:21:15,700
He went and prayed.

234
00:21:16,900 --> 00:21:21,220
Simon and his companions went to look for him, and when they found him, they exclaimed,

235
00:21:21,220 --> 00:21:23,260
Everyone is looking for you.

236
00:21:23,260 --> 00:21:25,720
Whew.

237
00:21:25,720 --> 00:21:27,900
Demons.

238
00:21:33,500 --> 00:21:35,780
You can almost hear it in the disciples' voices.

239
00:21:35,780 --> 00:21:37,980
What are you doing out here alone with God?

240
00:21:37,980 --> 00:21:41,000
There's a crowd back there waiting for you.

241
00:21:41,000 --> 00:21:42,800
We're doing this thing.

242
00:21:42,800 --> 00:21:43,960
The Messiah, it's time.

243
00:21:43,960 --> 00:21:45,060
Right?

244
00:21:45,060 --> 00:21:48,460
Jesus replied, I love this.

245
00:21:48,460 --> 00:21:50,920
Let us go somewhere else.

246
00:21:52,820 --> 00:21:55,280
To the nearby villages, so I can preach there also.

247
00:21:55,280 --> 00:21:57,200
This is why I have come.

248
00:21:57,200 --> 00:22:01,640
So he traveled throughout Galilee, preaching in their synagogues.

249
00:22:01,640 --> 00:22:05,720
I don't want to miss this.

250
00:22:05,720 --> 00:22:07,640
This is where the story begins to shift.

251
00:22:07,640 --> 00:22:13,440
Up to this point, Jesus is doing everything exactly the way the crowds and his disciples were.

252
00:22:15,760 --> 00:22:20,920
He's teaching with authority, casting out demons, and feeling sick, and he's gathering a mass to follow.

253
00:22:20,920 --> 00:22:25,000
The disciples likely go to bed that night with excitement in their bones.

254
00:22:25,000 --> 00:22:26,940
They've got the momentum.

255
00:22:26,940 --> 00:22:28,360
They've got the crowd.

256
00:22:28,360 --> 00:22:29,880
Their popularity is growing.

257
00:22:29,880 --> 00:22:37,840
Let's keep this ship rolling, and at this pace, we will overthrow Rome in a few months and restore Israel to its rightful plan.

258
00:22:38,980 --> 00:22:49,000
This is the culture of the people of God waiting for the Messiah, and the disciples get up with excitement in their bones to get to work only to find Jesus gone.

259
00:22:49,000 --> 00:22:58,360
In this fast-paced narrative of ministry success, Jesus withdraws into the Eremos, the solitude, the desert place, to pray.

260
00:22:59,300 --> 00:23:09,400
And this is the place where Jesus regularly goes to encounter the Heavenly Father and where the will and ways of God in heaven come into tension with the will and ways of the disciples.

261
00:23:09,400 --> 00:23:19,440
There's this tension point in solitude with God where what the disciples and the crowds want come into tension with what Jesus and the Father.

262
00:23:19,440 --> 00:23:28,880
There's a different strategy at play when we get away into the solitude and spend time with God than the strategy of the crowds in the world.

263
00:23:29,300 --> 00:23:33,100
All the disciples come to Him pretty much angry.

264
00:23:33,100 --> 00:23:38,120
Mark gives us some subtle clues that they are really dropping the ball here.

265
00:23:38,120 --> 00:23:43,260
The term went to look for Him is a way that suggests aggressive undertones.

266
00:23:43,260 --> 00:23:46,000
It can also be translated, they hunt Him down.

267
00:23:46,000 --> 00:23:47,120
Right?

268
00:23:47,120 --> 00:23:54,820
The disciples that have just started following Jesus not too long ago are hunting Him down to tell Him what He should and shouldn't be doing.

269
00:23:54,820 --> 00:23:59,000
As He's alone with the Father in solitude and prayer.

270
00:23:59,900 --> 00:24:06,920
The verb, this one's fun, the verb used for looking, Mark uses it six other times in the book of Mark.

271
00:24:06,920 --> 00:24:10,820
And every time it's used, it's used with people who have negative intentions.

272
00:24:10,820 --> 00:24:15,020
His family come looking for Him because they think He's nuts.

273
00:24:15,020 --> 00:24:20,340
Pharisees are demanding or looking for a sign.

274
00:24:20,340 --> 00:24:22,480
Sadducees are looking to put Him to death.

275
00:24:22,580 --> 00:24:29,500
Mark is very clearly telling us that there is a division between what the disciples want for Jesus and for what Jesus wants for Him.

276
00:24:29,500 --> 00:24:35,360
It's in the place of solitude where the strategy of the kingdom of God comes into tension.

277
00:24:36,100 --> 00:24:41,440
Between what God's followers want and what God wants of His followers.

278
00:24:41,440 --> 00:24:46,560
The disciples brush into Christ's time of solitude with confusion.

279
00:24:46,560 --> 00:24:52,320
Why would you be alone in the desert when we've got a crowd of people ready for you to continue your messianic?

280
00:24:53,920 --> 00:24:58,440
They were desperate for Him to be Messiah, for God's kingdom to come to earth.

281
00:24:58,440 --> 00:25:04,940
They could only see it through their own lenses, which were influenced by the world and the flesh.

282
00:25:04,940 --> 00:25:09,820
It was influenced by the cultural ideas of power and influence.

283
00:25:09,820 --> 00:25:12,360
How do movements pick up steam?

284
00:25:12,360 --> 00:25:14,580
They pick up steam with popularity, crowds.

285
00:25:15,400 --> 00:25:18,900
They pick up steam by saying the right things to the right people in the right spaces.

286
00:25:18,900 --> 00:25:20,820
It's very strategic, very intentional.

287
00:25:20,820 --> 00:25:26,000
And the disciples want Jesus to operate with this type of wisdom.

288
00:25:26,000 --> 00:25:29,800
Not only that, but they come to Him from a fleshly desire.

289
00:25:29,800 --> 00:25:33,200
They want things to go their way so that they can become popular.

290
00:25:33,200 --> 00:25:39,420
They were thinking, I'm giving up everything because I'm going to be one of the right-hand guys for the Messiah.

291
00:25:39,420 --> 00:25:40,960
I'm going to be in on the ground floor.

292
00:25:40,960 --> 00:25:45,860
I'm going to get all the benefits of being part of one of the most influential movements in human history.

293
00:25:45,860 --> 00:25:48,160
They understood the goal.

294
00:25:48,160 --> 00:25:55,780
But the strategy is significantly different from Jesus and from the disciples.

295
00:25:55,780 --> 00:25:57,240
I'm proud.

296
00:25:57,240 --> 00:26:03,200
And it's when Jesus enters solitude where these things become intention.

297
00:26:03,200 --> 00:26:05,040
I love how Dr. Tim Gombas puts it.

298
00:26:05,040 --> 00:26:12,140
It says, while Jesus' agenda, His goal, His purpose is to establish God's kingdom rule,

299
00:26:12,140 --> 00:26:15,360
His method or His strategy is dramatically different.

300
00:26:15,360 --> 00:26:19,380
The Son of God ushers in God's reign through suffering and through death.

301
00:26:19,380 --> 00:26:23,540
And His ministry will fly in the face of cultural expectations.

302
00:26:23,540 --> 00:26:30,740
The strategy by which God brings about His kingdom will fly in the face of the world and the flesh.

303
00:26:31,440 --> 00:26:36,220
This difficult mission is the reason Jesus is in the desert to pray.

304
00:26:36,220 --> 00:26:40,400
To bring His strategy in alignment with the will of the Father.

305
00:26:40,400 --> 00:26:46,640
To get away from the pressures of the world and what they want for Him.

306
00:26:46,640 --> 00:26:48,600
And to get with the Father.

307
00:26:48,600 --> 00:26:50,900
To abide in the Eremos with the Father.

308
00:26:50,900 --> 00:26:52,980
And to keep in step with His will and His way.

309
00:26:52,980 --> 00:26:54,400
I love how John 6 puts it.

310
00:26:55,660 --> 00:27:01,120
Jesus says, for I have come down from heaven not to do my will, but to do the will of Him who sent me.

311
00:27:01,120 --> 00:27:05,000
Jesus is fully God and fully man.

312
00:27:05,000 --> 00:27:10,520
There is probably part of the fully man in Him that says, the crowd thing sounds nice.

313
00:27:10,520 --> 00:27:11,720
Right?

314
00:27:11,720 --> 00:27:14,500
The momentum thing, the popularity thing, that sounds nice.

315
00:27:14,500 --> 00:27:19,020
But it's in solitude where He continues to surrender His will to the Father's will.

316
00:27:19,220 --> 00:27:22,860
He continues to do things the way the Father invites Him to do them.

317
00:27:22,860 --> 00:27:30,900
As we will see throughout the rest of Christ's life, the will of the Father flies from the face of the will of the crowds and even His sight.

318
00:27:33,160 --> 00:27:37,960
And this is why Jesus invites us in solitude to pray.

319
00:27:37,960 --> 00:27:45,280
So that we can begin to encounter God and understand His will and His ways that are in opposition to our own.

320
00:27:45,280 --> 00:27:47,000
Here's my main point.

321
00:27:47,000 --> 00:27:47,640
That's what I would say.

322
00:27:47,640 --> 00:27:53,080
Solitude is a place where we encounter God and actively surrender to His will and His will.

323
00:27:56,040 --> 00:28:04,400
It's a place where we can begin to realize that what God is inviting us into might be a little bit different than how we would do it if we were in charge.

324
00:28:04,400 --> 00:28:10,680
The life and example of Jesus shows us God's strategy for establishing His kingdom.

325
00:28:10,680 --> 00:28:16,340
And it's far different than any worldly strategy for a successful movement.

326
00:28:16,340 --> 00:28:19,640
1 Corinthians 3.

327
00:28:19,640 --> 00:28:25,300
The cross is foolishness to those who are perishing.

328
00:28:26,040 --> 00:28:29,560
But to us who are being saved, it is the very power of God.

329
00:28:29,560 --> 00:28:33,880
A cross?

330
00:28:33,880 --> 00:28:36,960
A bloody Messiah?

331
00:28:36,960 --> 00:28:38,620
A suffering servant?

332
00:28:38,620 --> 00:28:41,560
Makes no sense.

333
00:28:41,560 --> 00:28:49,020
The crowds and the disciples wanted a powerful king on a war horse with a sword.

334
00:28:49,020 --> 00:28:52,880
They got a humble servant on a donkey.

335
00:28:54,940 --> 00:29:02,180
And it's in solitude with God where we allow Him to correct the ways in which we want to accomplish His purposes.

336
00:29:02,180 --> 00:29:04,980
But we want to do it on our agenda.

337
00:29:04,980 --> 00:29:07,160
At our pace.

338
00:29:07,160 --> 00:29:08,220
With our desire.

339
00:29:08,220 --> 00:29:14,720
And oftentimes, if we're not careful, we'll get so frustrated that we'll flip the lid and we'll begin to make shortcuts.

340
00:29:16,400 --> 00:29:20,240
We'll begin to do ministry based on business principles of the world.

341
00:29:20,240 --> 00:29:22,500
And yeah, we might see some fruitfulness at the beginning.

342
00:29:24,040 --> 00:29:30,820
But if we're accomplishing God's purposes with the wisdom of the world and not the wisdom of the cross, that those purposes will not last.

343
00:29:30,820 --> 00:29:32,700
They will not flourish.

344
00:29:35,920 --> 00:29:38,040
The disciples wanted a conquering king.

345
00:29:38,040 --> 00:29:39,100
They got a suffering servant.

346
00:29:39,100 --> 00:29:42,360
And then one of my favorite new images in the Bible.

347
00:29:43,480 --> 00:29:45,020
I've told you guys this before.

348
00:29:45,020 --> 00:29:46,240
All transparency.

349
00:29:46,240 --> 00:29:48,600
I have avoided the book of Revelation like the plague.

350
00:29:48,600 --> 00:29:52,620
But I'm starting to dip my toes in the water.

351
00:29:52,620 --> 00:29:57,540
And one of the most beautiful visions in the book of Revelation sums up this point so well.

352
00:29:58,920 --> 00:30:03,300
It's the climax of this heavenly throne room vision.

353
00:30:03,300 --> 00:30:04,780
It's all political language.

354
00:30:04,780 --> 00:30:06,460
There's a throne room of God.

355
00:30:06,460 --> 00:30:11,100
And there's a scroll with God's redemptive plan for creation written on it.

356
00:30:11,100 --> 00:30:12,840
And it's sealed with seven seals.

357
00:30:12,840 --> 00:30:17,140
And there's no one in heaven and on earth who is worthy to open the seal.

358
00:30:17,140 --> 00:30:19,320
To break the seals and to open the scroll.

359
00:30:19,320 --> 00:30:21,460
This is so political.

360
00:30:21,460 --> 00:30:28,000
This is we are waiting for a powerful leader who can do the thing we've been waiting for God to do for us.

361
00:30:28,080 --> 00:30:30,700
We're waiting for this powerful leader to come.

362
00:30:30,700 --> 00:30:34,020
And John hears an angel tell him, don't worry.

363
00:30:34,020 --> 00:30:37,840
Behold the lion, the lion from the tribe of Judah.

364
00:30:37,840 --> 00:30:38,520
Now.

365
00:30:38,520 --> 00:30:40,640
That makes sense.

366
00:30:40,640 --> 00:30:43,920
A roaring lion.

367
00:30:43,920 --> 00:30:48,020
It's time.

368
00:30:48,020 --> 00:30:51,560
Powerful God is going to come and do the thing.

369
00:30:51,560 --> 00:30:58,060
And then John looks to see what he thinks is going to be a powerful lion coming to do the thing that they've been waiting to do.

370
00:30:58,080 --> 00:31:05,520
And instead of seeing a lion, he sees a little lamb as though it was slain.

371
00:31:08,440 --> 00:31:10,320
And all of heaven rejoices.

372
00:31:10,320 --> 00:31:16,840
Because that is the strategy by which God brings about his kingdom redemption plan.

373
00:31:16,840 --> 00:31:22,720
It's not through power or control or through political affiliation.

374
00:31:22,720 --> 00:31:28,400
It's not through voting in the right people to do the thing that you want them to do.

375
00:31:28,480 --> 00:31:31,760
It's through laying down your life sacrificially with love.

376
00:31:31,760 --> 00:31:33,200
It's through looking to Jesus.

377
00:31:33,200 --> 00:31:35,860
Following his example.

378
00:31:39,860 --> 00:31:45,560
The lamb who is able to break the seals and open the scroll.

379
00:31:45,560 --> 00:31:56,780
God's strategy of his kingdom, of his building his kingdom purposes, stands in stark contrast to the wisdom of the world and to the desires of our flesh.

380
00:31:56,780 --> 00:31:57,820
We don't want surrender.

381
00:31:58,780 --> 00:32:00,220
We don't want sacrifice.

382
00:32:00,220 --> 00:32:03,080
We want influence.

383
00:32:03,080 --> 00:32:04,100
We want control.

384
00:32:04,100 --> 00:32:06,480
We want to be on the winning team.

385
00:32:06,480 --> 00:32:13,360
And in solitude, we have this invitation to withdraw from the world.

386
00:32:13,360 --> 00:32:15,920
To withdraw from the desires of our flesh.

387
00:32:15,920 --> 00:32:19,440
And to let God dictate what success looks like.

388
00:32:20,140 --> 00:32:24,400
What his strategy actually is for accomplishing his purpose.

389
00:32:24,400 --> 00:32:31,240
I think most of us in the room are like the disciples and the crowds.

390
00:32:31,240 --> 00:32:33,220
We're desperate for God's kingdom to come.

391
00:32:33,220 --> 00:32:37,560
We've seen him show up in our lives and in the lives of those around us.

392
00:32:37,560 --> 00:32:48,780
But my concern is I'm afraid that the way in which we want to partner with him to see his work done is far more often based on our desires and worldly wisdom.

393
00:32:49,460 --> 00:32:51,520
Than it is the cross.

394
00:32:51,520 --> 00:32:53,240
The lamb who is.

395
00:32:53,240 --> 00:33:01,500
We want to cultivate God's kingdom in partnership with political powers and a popular message that can gather crowds.

396
00:33:01,500 --> 00:33:05,520
But what if Jesus is actually inviting us to pick up a cross and follow?

397
00:33:05,520 --> 00:33:17,320
What if kingdom building actually means this church gets smaller and smaller because we get more and more serious about doing the thing that he's inviting us to do the way he's inviting us to do?

398
00:33:18,780 --> 00:33:27,180
It's not a message that draws crowds if the crowds are wanting to live by the wisdom of the world.

399
00:33:29,280 --> 00:33:34,860
But, for those who are being saved, it is the very power of God.

400
00:33:34,860 --> 00:33:40,440
There's only one way.

401
00:33:40,440 --> 00:33:45,600
Only one way I can properly get Rory to play with this story.

402
00:33:47,460 --> 00:33:53,480
And it's if I can just get him to calm down enough to lock eyes on me.

403
00:33:53,480 --> 00:33:59,320
And I hand him the shape and I spin the wheel right in front of him.

404
00:34:00,320 --> 00:34:04,080
And I almost have to guide his hand to put the shape in the truck.

405
00:34:04,080 --> 00:34:10,860
And I think that's a picture of what solitude can be for us.

406
00:34:12,300 --> 00:34:20,500
Solitude can be a place where we can lock eyes with God, knowing what the goal is, fully knowing that we want to see his kingdom come and his will be done.

407
00:34:22,160 --> 00:34:36,520
And instead of getting frustrated, taking shortcuts, solitude is an invitation for us to lock eyes with God and for him to show us how to go about accomplishing his purposes and his will come.

408
00:34:38,860 --> 00:34:44,700
And the beauty of the truck for the kingdom of God is it's a much simpler strategy.

409
00:34:44,700 --> 00:34:47,040
This truck has multiple shapes.

410
00:34:47,040 --> 00:34:51,100
The kingdom of God truck has only one shape.

411
00:34:51,100 --> 00:34:53,320
The shape of the cross.

412
00:34:53,320 --> 00:35:00,520
The kingdom of God accomplishes its purposes through sacrificial love, through laying down our life for the sake of the gospel.

413
00:35:00,520 --> 00:35:06,800
